A||N||11||willempie||high idle at 3000 RPM||||8||
Z||000000||willempie||11-30-2001||04:51 AM||||hey guys i am new here, but i am a real fiero fan! i have a 85 notchback GT V6. Only one problem the idle is tooo high. When i start the car it begins at 2300Rpm and gets higher after runner a while up to 3000RPM. We have replaced the IAC and we can not find any vacuum leaks, i dont know what to do, please help me! When i unplug the IAC and then set the ignition ON it doesnt move very much and very slow, could there be a loose connection??? <P><P>------------------<BR>Willem Sanders <BR>willemvespa@hotmail.com||||reg||8
Z||000001||RossT||11-30-2001||06:06 AM||||First thing is click on the "ogre's" link at top of page and read the vacuum leak section!<P>Second thing is search this forum using "high idle" or like terms.<P>A steady high idle is almost always a vac. leak. Most of the time it is the EGR tube or EGR valve or solinoid. I used a dental miror<BR>to find a small crack in my egr tube that was causing my high idle.<P>could be several other things but start with the above first!<P>good luck!||||reg||1
Z||000002||2farnorth||11-30-2001||06:11 AM||||First of all welcome to THE FORUM.  You'll find lots of good people and information here.  As for your high idle, take close look at the EGR tube.  I think you'll find that it's cracked or broken off near where fastens to the intake.  Good luck.<P>Dave||||reg||1
Z||000003||willempie||11-30-2001||06:52 AM||||We have already checked the egr tube and everything seemed to be ok. the valve worked fine so this shouldn't be the problem. Any other solutions?<P>------------------<BR>Willem Sanders <BR>willemvespa@hotmail.com||||reg||9
Z||000004||DJWINNI||11-30-2001||07:22 AM||||Hi Willempie!<BR> I'm a 19 years old french and I've bought a 1986 Fiero. By now, I've the same problem than you!! I've change the EGR valve which was damaged but I still have that problem. I'v checked all the black little plastic hoses and I've found one which was not connected. Otherwise, it should be the EGR tube or the EGR valve. But as you said, yours are correct.It can be the sensor too. The TPS, the MAP, or the IAC.<BR> I will let you know if I achieve to repair my trouble, so long, good luck!!<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000005||Indiana_resto_guy||11-30-2001||08:30 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by willempie:<BR><B>We have already checked the egr tube and everything seemed to be ok. the valve worked fine so this shouldn't be the problem. Any other solutions?<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>First of all Welcome to the Forum to you and to DJWINNI!<BR>This reply pertains to the both of you in part.<BR>Are either of you getting any codes besides a high idle?<BR>Willempie, when the EGR tube was checked, were both ends checked as well as the middle? It happens that the tube can crack in the middle under the heat wrap but not often. Next the EGR Valve, how did you check it? Plunger operation or vacuum check? How about the solenoid?<BR>There are several vacuum lines, both soft, which can deteriorate, and hard plastic that cracks. There are also steel lines that can suck large amounts of air if rusted as well. Two smaller ones that run the cruise control,  a large line for the brake booster and the booster itself. Also the cruise control can may be rusted.<BR>All of them need to be checked individually.<BR>Many things can be a source of vacuum leaks as you can see.<BR>Keep us posted of your progress.<P><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000006||DJWINNI||11-30-2001||11:04 AM||||i've tried to solve the problem and it still doesn't work!<BR>I'm lost as you!!!!<P>------------------<BR> <A HREF="http://pageperso.aol.fr/djwinnimic/djwinnifierosignature.jpg" TARGET=_blank>http://pageperso.aol.fr/djwinnimic/djwinnifierosignature.jpg</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000007||StuGood||11-30-2001||12:59 PM||||My favorite way to detect vacuum leaks in the V6 Fiero is to start the car, get a piece of hose, put one end up to my ear and go "exploring" with the other end - around the plenum, EGR tube, etc.  In other words, use the hose as a stethoscope.   <P>When you bring the hose near a vacuum leak, the sound is unmistakable: "Psssst!"  You'll know it when you hear it.<P>For example, my GT used to idle too fast when I bought it.  I used the method above to find a vacuum leak, where the EGR tube connects underneath the plenum.  "Psssst!," it said.  It was obvious where the vacuum leak was.  As it turned out, the gasket was improperly installed - it only picked up one of the 2 bolts.  The rest of the gasket was sticking out from bewteen the EGR tube and plenum!<P>Apparently, whoever worked on it last didn't have the patience to get the tube flange (which can rotate about the tube), and gasket  lined up with the holes in the plenum.  So I took it apart and installed the tube properly.  Problem solved! And it cost nothing but a little time and patience...<P>Anyway, like the others posted, vacuum leak(s) would be the prime suspect, in my opinion.  Good luck  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000008||willempie||12-05-2001||06:30 AM||||ok i have checked the EGR now but havent been able to find anything, anyone some other ideas?<P>------------------<BR>Willem Sanders <BR>willemvespa@hotmail.com||||reg||9
Z||000009||NEPTUNE||12-06-2001||10:38 AM||||My EGRr tube was bad but looked like new. (same symptoms)-there was a little hole where the upper flange connects to the tube. No way to see it. <BR>EASY WAY TO CHECK IT:<BR>Remove the rubber air intake hose, open the throttle, spray 1/3 can of carb cleaner into the throttlebody. Look for a drip or wet spot around the egr tube area. ||||reg||3
Z||000010||willempie||12-07-2001||04:45 AM||||thx, i will try it!<P>------------------<BR>Willem Sanders <BR>willemvespa@hotmail.com||||reg||6
Z||000011||DJWINNI||12-07-2001||12:48 PM||||Hi! Now, I'm totally lost with my Fiero. My idle problem is still not resolved. In fact, the prob is that my idle is about 3000-3500 RPM, but if I disconnect the plastic hose going from the MAP to the Fuel Pressure Regulation situated underneath th red spider, the idle drops to 1500-2000RPM. Where is the real problem???? Can someone PLEASE help me?<BR>Thanks a lot!<P>------------------<BR> <A HREF="http://pageperso.aol.fr/djwinnimic/djwinnifierosignature.jpg" TARGET=_blank>pageperso.aol.fr/djwinnimic/djwinnifierosignature.jpg</A> ||||reg||1
